Resolved Resonance Region (RRR)   1.e-5 eV < En < 2.554 keV       7328 1451   44
                                                                  7328 1451   45
D. Barry (NNL), J. Brown (ORNL), M. Pigni (ORNL), A. Lewis (NNL)  7328 1451   46
 --------------------------------------------------------------   7328 1451   47
                                                                  7328 1451   48
 The RRR parameters were generated by the fit of experimental     7328 1451   49
 transmission and capture data sets [ref01-05] using the          7328 1451   50
 SAMMY code [ref06].                                              7328 1451   51
                                                                  7328 1451   52
 The evaluation procedure involved extending the ENDF/B-VIII.0    7328 1451   53
 library [ref07] RRR parameters from 330 eV to ~2.5 keV. The      7328 1451   54
 initial (prior) RRR parameters from 0 eV through ~2.5 keV used   7328 1451   55
 in the SAMMY Bayesian fit were taken from the JEFF-3.3 library   7328 1451   56
 [ref08].                                                         7328 1451   57
                                                                  7328 1451   58
 Total angular momentum of the resonance states, J, were set to   7328 1451   59
 the values found in the ATLAS [ref09]. Where the ATLAS did not   7328 1451   60
 list the value of J, the values were assigned using a Monte      7328 1451   61
 Carlo method.                                                    7328 1451   62
                                                                  7328 1451   63
 To improve resonance statistics, 59 small ficticious resonances  7328 1451   64
 were added using a Monte Carlo method. These ficticious          7328 1451   65
 resonances can be found at the following energies (eV):          7328 1451   66
                                                                  7328 1451   67
     777.7576, 1176.2002, 1194.2424, 1272.3558, 1416.7815,        7328 1451   68
    1609.2861, 1617.9175, 1631.1783, 1684.5230, 1710.6119,        7328 1451   69
    1778.8005, 1780.4021, 1821.8993, 1844.4009, 1854.1086,        7328 1451   70
    1909.8719, 1917.5191, 1927.0588, 1937.6194, 1969.1251,        7328 1451   71
    1979.0537, 1981.8120, 2001.9080, 2084.9294, 2120.7235,        7328 1451   72
    2140.2814, 2153.4697, 2157.5253, 2172.1997, 2173.7465,        7328 1451   73
    2179.6965, 2207.9018, 2222.4742, 2246.1298, 2251.9046,        7328 1451   74
    2262.3530, 2269.8958, 2294.6264, 2310.9100, 2322.7412,        7328 1451   75
    2338.9572, 2361.7914, 2380.7800, 2384.5895, 2385.5723,        7328 1451   76
    2386.4223, 2412.4421, 2418.6198, 2433.0732, 2443.0639,        7328 1451   77
    2453.4527, 2456.6754, 2463.7564, 2488.0721, 2497.5018,        7328 1451   78
    2501.1531, 2518.0952, 2526.7661, 2534.6699                    7328 1451   79
                                                                  7328 1451   80
 The RRR covariances were also generatated using SAMMY. This      7328 1451   81
 covariance information is included in File 32 using the LCOMP=1  7328 1451   82
 format.                                                          7328 1451   83
                                                                  7328 1451   84
 The thermal cross section values were calculated using           7328 1451   85
 NJOY [ref10] and INTER [ref11]. A Monte Carlo method was used    7328 1451   86
 to generate the estimated uncertainties (not including           7328 1451   87
 covariances).                                                    7328 1451   88
                                                                  7328 1451   89
