 Unresolved Resonance Region (URR)  2.554 keV < En < 100 keV      7328 1451  128
                                                                  7328 1451  129
 D. Barry (NNL), J. Brown (ORNL), M. Pigni (ORNL), A. Lewis (NNL) 7328 1451  130
 --------------------------------------------------------------   7328 1451  131
 The URR evaluation used the mean values of resonance parameters  7328 1451  132
 and uncertainties from the RRR and propagated them to the URR    7328 1451  133
 prior. Average cross section data was fit to obtain the          7328 1451  134
 posterior average resonance parameters and covariance. File 3    7328 1451  135
 cross sections for the URR region were generated with SAMMY from 7328 1451  136
 the posterior parameters in the URR.                             7328 1451  137
                                                                  7328 1451  138
 The Bayesian fitting code SAMMY/FITACS was used to generate      7328 1451  139
 posterior mean values and covariances for average resonance      7328 1451  140
 parameters: neutron strength function S_l, average gamma-gamma   7328 1451  141
 <G_g>, and distant-level parameter R_inf. These are used to      7328 1451  142
 calculate average neutron width, average capture width, average  7328 1451  143
 competitive width (only the first inelastic state <100 keV) and  7328 1451  144
 average level spacing as a function of energy to match the       7328 1451  145
 ENDF/B format, as well as the mean values of cross sections      7328 1451  146
 placed in File 3. The prior parameter distributions for Bayes'   7328 1451  147
 equation are determined from the final fitted RRR parameters     7328 1451  148
 described above between 0-330 eV (note that this is a subset of  7328 1451  149
 the full RRR). Average level spacing <D> = 4.1 eV. The L=1 and   7328 1451  150
 L=2 distant level parameters must be set to the L=0 distant      7328 1451  151
 level parameter due to the limitations of ENDF. Inelastic states 7328 1451  152
 are from ENSDF [ref15], binding energy from Mughabghab et al.    7328 1451  153
 [ref09]. Pairing energy of zero is used as described by G&C      7328 1451  154
 [ref16]. Neutron separation energy of 6.06296 MeV was used.      7328 1451  155
 Prior values of S_l and <G_g> for l=1 and l=2 are from [ref09].  7328 1451  156
 Capture data included in analysis are from [ref02] and EXFOR     7328 1451  157
 [ref17-24]. Total cross section data are from [ref02] and EXFOR  7328 1451  158
 [ref25-26]. Total elastic cross section data are from [ref27].   7328 1451  159
                                                                  7328 1451  160
