                                                                  7328 1451  276
 OVERALL EVALUATION CONCEPT AND PROCEDURE                         7328 1451  277
                                                                  7328 1451  278
 This evaluation is seeking consistency among differential        7328 1451  279
 experimental data and nuclear reaction modeling and is a         7328 1451  280
 posteriori validated against integral experiments. It starts     7328 1451  281
 with selecting trustworthy and consistent set of experiments     7328 1451  282
 that define total cross sections in the whole energy range.      7328 1451  283
 This set is supported by additional experiments that after       7328 1451  284
 modest (a couple of %) normalization agree with the initial set. 7328 1451  285
 Such combined set is used to adjust optical model parameters     7328 1451  286
 providing the most critical base for the evaluation. Similar     7328 1451  287
 procedure is applied for other reactions as long as there        7328 1451  288
 is enough experimental data to define reliable shape of the      7328 1451  289
 excitation function.  If this is not the case, the most          7328 1451  290
 trusted experiments are given the priority over the average      7328 1451  291
 of all experimental data.                                        7328 1451  292
 Next, one MSD model parameter is varied to reproduce             7328 1451  293
 neutron spectra which, in case of Ta181, are                     7328 1451  294
 profusely available.  Cross sections for cluster emission are    7328 1451  295
 constraining exciton model parameters.                           7328 1451  296
 The only exception to this procedure is capture for which        7328 1451  297
 most trusted and accurate data were followed by means of         7328 1451  298
 energy dependent scaling of the capture gamma-width in the       7328 1451  299
 EMPIRE input.                                                    7328 1451  300
 Final refinement of the parameters is obtained by running        7328 1451  301
 Kalman filter on the selected set of adopted experiments.        7328 1451  302
 These calculations provide also covariances.                     7328 1451  303
 As the result, the evaluation is given entirely by the model     7328 1451  304
 calculation with the adjusted set of parameters and is fully     7328 1451  305
 reproducible.                                                    7328 1451  306
                                                                  7328 1451  307
                                                                  7328 1451  308
                                                                  7328 1451  309
         Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta           7328 1451  310
                         (SVN rev. 5361 )                         7328 1451  311
                  M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                 7328 1451  312
                                                                  7328 1451  313
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 7328 1451  314
 NDNUC= 100  NDEXCLUS= 50  NDEX= 201  NDLW=  60                   7328 1451  315
 LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                         7328 1451  316
                                                                  7328 1451  317
                                                                  7328 1451  318
 This code integrates into a single system a number               7328 1451  319
 of important modules and features:                               7328 1451  320
                                                                  7328 1451  321
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 7328 1451  322
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      7328 1451  323
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  7328 1451  324
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                7328 1451  325
   and coworkers                                                  7328 1451  326
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                7328 1451  327
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       7328 1451  328
 - Quantum-mechanical MSC NVWY model                              7328 1451  329
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      7328 1451  330
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 7328 1451  331
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                7328 1451  332
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               7328 1451  333
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                7328 1451  334
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    7328 1451  335
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          7328 1451  336
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 7328 1451  337
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   7328 1451  338
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                7328 1451  339
   discrete transitions                                           7328 1451  340
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                7328 1451  341
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                7328 1451  342
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               7328 1451  343
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 7328 1451  344
   library [RIPL]                                                 7328 1451  345
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              7328 1451  346
   EXFOR library                                                  7328 1451  347
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     7328 1451  348
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 7328 1451  349
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                7328 1451  350
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      7328 1451  351
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   7328 1451  352
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      7328 1451  353
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   7328 1451  354
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  7328 1451  355
 - generating covariances                                         7328 1451  356
 - Support for NJOY                                               7328 1451  357
                                                                  7328 1451  358
