  Preequilibrium emission                                         7328 1451  396
  =======================                                         7328 1451  397
 Three reaction models were used to describe emission from the    7328 1451  398
 composite Ta182 nucleus prior to attaining equilibrium.          7328 1451  399
                                                                  7328 1451  400
 TUL MultiStep Direct model (MSD) was used for unbound neutron in 7328 1451  401
 in the incident channel prior to MultiStep Compound emission.    7328 1451  402
 Field strength for l = 0 transfer was fitted to GMR at           7328 1451  403
 6.380 MeV to reproduce high energy part of neutron spectra.      7328 1451  404
                                                                  7328 1451  405
 Heidelberg MultiStep Compound (MSC) calculations were used for   7328 1451  406
 preequilibrium neutron, proton and gamma emission including      7328 1451  407
 contribution to discrete levels.  Default parameters were used.  7328 1451  408
                                                                  7328 1451  409
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS including            7328 1451  410
 cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model and        7328 1451  411
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1) were      7328 1451  412
 employed for modeling cluster preequilibrium.                    7328 1451  413
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS was set to  0.8 (Recomm:~1.5) 7328 1451  414
 and PE emission width of tritons from 182Ta were scaled by  0.3  7328 1451  415
 in order to reproduce experimental data.                         7328 1451  416
                                                                  7328 1451  417
            Use of direct and preequilibrium models               7328 1451  418
