  Compound Nucleus                                                7328 1451  439
  ================                                                7328 1451  440
 Standard Hauser-Feshbach statistical model with account for      7328 1451  441
 Moldauer width fluctuation correction was used.                  7328 1451  442
 Tlj coupling up to incident 3.00 MeV was used.                   7328 1451  443
 CN decay and Direct cross sections were added incoherently.      7328 1451  444
 CN anisotropy was calculated using Blatt-Biedenharn coefficients.7328 1451  445
 Traditional approach to calculate transmission coefficients      7328 1451  446
 Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs) was adopted.                         7328 1451  447
 E1 strength function was set to RIPL MLO1 model.                 7328 1451  448
 GDR parameters from RIPL/Exp.data & Plujko systematics were      7328 1451  449
 used for determining gamma-strength functions.                   7328 1451  450
 Maximum gamma-transition multipolarity was set to 2.             7328 1451  451
 Gamma emission width was made energy dependent to fit (n,g).     7328 1451  452
                                                                  7328 1451  453
 Gilbert-Cameron (EMPIRE 2.18) level densities were adopted       7328 1451  454
 and matched to reproduce cumulative numbers of discrete levels,  7328 1451  455
 which were taken from the RIPL-3+ library based on the 2015      7328 1451  456
 version of ENSDF.  Cut-off energies for level densities are:     7328 1451  457
